
1. install angular using npm using below command
    npm install -g @angular/cli

2. Once installed, use below command to create a new angular project
    ng new blogproject

3. To run angular project
    ng serve

4. Create components using : ng g component <componentname>
    1. appheader component
    2. Main component

5. To use bootstrap
    Download the component like nav code from below website
        https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.0/getting-started/introduction/
    Add cdn into head tag of html

6. Routing
    Whatever component we want to show or navigate will be inputted into <router-outlet></router-outlet> tag.
    This tag will be present inside app.html
    routerlink='/about'

7. We will use reactive form here 
    Add ReactiveFormsModule, FormsModule module in app.module.ts

8. Install json-server
    npm i -g json-server

    This json-server is used to use dummy api and dummy data.
    We will use  our backend server which i created using springboot.

9. Create a service
    Create a services folder and create a service component
    ng g s Services/service

10. To use http, check below points
    -> import {HttpClient} in the component
    -> create objcet of HttpClient inside constructor argument
    -> Import HttpClientModule in app.module.ts file
    -> Add HttpClientModule in he imports section

11. How to make the form responsive
    Add whole content in div with below class
    <div class="col-sm-6 mx-auto">

12. Create component to show blog datas
    ng g c home
    here we will show the all available blogs in cards
    each card will be having link to content, for this we used <a> tag within span

13. lets create blog component
    This component will show the content of each blog .
    Whenever user click on content link to view that blog then he will be redirected to this page.
    ng g c blog-content

14. Whenever we want to route the url path like blog/id, then we are routing in below way in routing.module.ts
    {path:'blog/:id', component:BlogContentComponent}

15. To get any url paramter, we need one module named as ActivatedRoute.
    Import this ActivatedRoute in component.
    Create object of this ActivatedRoute within constructor parameter.

16. If after submission need to route to another page then use below
    import { Router } from '@angular/router';
    this.navigate.navigateByUrl('routePathHere');
